  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.5.0: Adds the context-overflow vocabulary shared by every provider. ContextLengthExceededException carries the model's window, the rejected prompt's size, the HTTP status and why recovery could not save the request. AIHttpErrorFactory translates a provider's HTTP failure into that exception (or a plain AIServiceException when the body says something else) and builds the metadata for streaming error chunks, so a consuming app learns that the context overflowed without learning how any particular vendor phrases it. Detection covers OpenAI, vLLM, Anthropic — including the combined \"input length and `max_tokens` exceed context limit\" form — and Google, and is gated to 400/413 so a rate limit or a server error is never mistaken for one. ChatBlock.RemoveFunctionMessages() is now marked for removal in v7.0. Additive minor release; no breaking changes.",
